WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Accelerate electrons in a vacuum through
a potential difference of up to about

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.800
150 kilovolts, and smash
them into tungsten.

3
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.360
Less than 1 per cent of their
energy comes out as X-rays.

4
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.770
The rest heats the target.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.100
Tungsten melts only at
about 3400 degrees Celsius,

6
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.900
and the target spins to
spread the heat round a ring.

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.420
So how does slamming electrons
into metal make X-rays at all?

8
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.220
In this mission, you'll
build the X-ray tube,

9
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.070
from hot filament to tungsten target.

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.730
Then you'll learn to control
the beam: how many photons,

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.850
and how penetrating they are.

12
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: explain how slamming
electrons into a lump of metal makes X-rays.
